RF.put("questb:b46",{"8846":{"id":8846,"t":"Five Signets for War Supplies","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Alliance Commendation Signet","desc":"Ah, here for additional supplies for yourself, are you? Well, I can certainly understand the need for additional materiel... just take a look around if you need any proof.\nI'll issue you some additional supplies, but you'll need to give me an appropriate number of commendation signets in exchange. You won't receive any recognition for surrendering the signets in this manner, but you might find something useful that will help keep you alive when battle is finally upon us.","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8526":{"id":8526,"t":"The Alliance Needs Roast Raptor!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 33.","obj":"Bring 20 Roast Raptor to Sarah Sadwhistle at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Roast Raptor","desc":"Oh, how's it going, ‹class›? I see that you're interested in maybe gathering up food for the coming war at Ahn'Qiraj? Somehow my dad thought that it would be a good learning experience for me if I were to volunteer to help out here. Big mistake. I don't even like to eat meat.\nAnyway, if you feel like it, you could bring me back a lot of roast raptor. Apparently that's what all of the soldiers are going to want.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"So do you have all of that roast raptor yet?","done":"Gee, that's swell. Thanks for bringing me all of this burnt animal flesh, ‹class›. I'll just put it onto the pile over there. I'm sure that someone will take care of it. I suppose if you have some time on your hands that you might want to bring me more?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.4,"n":"Sarah Sadwhistle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6846":{"id":6846,"t":"Begin the Attack!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Assault Orders","back":"My troops are supplied and ready to assault. We just need orders from Noreg Stormpike and I'll send them into the fray!","done":"Ah, the orders! They say I'm to assault at will, and my will says... now!\nStart Field Marshal Teravaine Alterac Valley End Field Marshal Teravaine Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6846","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7166":{"id":7166,"t":"Legendary Heroes","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Insignia Rank 4","desc":"Your radiate command and power, shaman. Exalted in the eyes of Frostwolf - the enemy cowers at the mention of your name.\nRise, Hero of Frostwolf. Rise and be honored!\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 5\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Your radiate command and power, ‹class›. Exalted in the eyes of Frostwolf - the enemy cowers at the mention of your name.\nRise, Hero of Frostwolf. Rise and be honored!\nPresent your insignia.","done":"Soon, all on the field of battle will be under your watchful eye. Command of the Valley and its troops will be yours!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7486":{"id":7486,"t":"A Hero's Reward","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 60.","obj":"Claim your reward from Hydraxis' Coffer.","desc":"‹name›, your services to the Warlords surpassed all we could expect from the denizens of this world.\nWe do not understand your people's notions of gratitude, or rewarding good works, but in this case... perhaps a reward is warranted.\nUnder the surf at the southern base of this island, you will find a coffer. In it you will find your... reward.\nGo, ‹name›. Claim your reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOcean's Breeze Tidal Loop\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Hydraxian Waterlords","done":"Hydraxis' voice descends from the waters' surface...\n\"Choose that which best suits you, ‹name›. May it protect you against the foes of the Waterlords.\"","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":79.2,"y":74.9,"n":"Hydraxis' Coffer","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4126":{"id":4126,"t":"Hurley Blackbreath","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 7,050 experience instead of 5,650, 1.25 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Lost Thunderbrew Recipe to Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos.\nLost Thunderbrew Recipe Blackbreath Crony , Hurley Blackbreath","desc":"The Dark Iron dwarves, led by the villain Hurley Blackbreath, stole one of the Thunderbrew's best recipes, Thunderbrew Lager. The villains! They don't deserve such a fine brew!\n‹name›, I have a tough task for you. Go to the Blackrock Depths in the Burning Steppes, destroy any kegs of Thunderbrew Lager you find, and bring back our recipe for Thunderbrew Lager!\nPlease, get that recipe back, even if you have to turn Blackrock Depths upside down to do it!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwiftstrike Cudgel Limb Cleaver\nYou will also receive:\n10 Dark Dwarven Lager\nMoney: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,050","back":"Do you have the recipe, ‹name›? I can't stand the idea of those Dark Iron dwarves drinking my family's drink!","done":"You found it! Well done! And I hope you gave those Dark Irons, and Hurley Blackbreath, a good thumping!\nThe Thunderbrews are at your service, ‹name›. You are a hero of heroes!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.8,"y":52.4,"n":"Ragnar Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4286":{"id":4286,"t":"The Good Stuff","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and recover 20 Dark Iron Fanny Packs. Return to Oralius when you have completed this task. You assume that the Dark Iron dwarves inside Blackrock Depths carry these 'fanny pack' contraptions.\n20 Dark Iron Fanny Pack Crest Killer 80 % , Blackbreath Crony 80 % , Watchman Doomgrip 80 % , Dark Guard 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Captain Winky tells me that the Dark Irons in the Depths got all the good stuff. Ain't that right, Winky?\n<Oralius does his best impersonation of a pirate.>\nARRR MATEY! IT BE RIGHT!\nSee what I'm saying? You need to get in there and bring me back some samples of the good stuff.\nGet in there and shake your moneymaker!","rew":"You will receive:\nA Dingy Fanny Pack\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I can't be bothered right now, ‹name›. Me and Winky got a meeting to attend.","done":"<Oralius starts rummaging through the mountainous pile of fanny packs.>\nOH WONDERFUL!\n<Oralius sticks his large nose into the pile and takes a whiff.>\nDELICIOUS! Look at all these goodies!\nTake one for yourself, ‹name›. There's plenty to go around.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Oralius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4766":{"id":4766,"t":"Mayara Brightwing","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mayara Brightwing in the Burning Steppes.","desc":"An agent of mine, Mayara Brightwing, was sent to the Burning Steppes to scout the ruined city of Thaurissan. That destroyed city of the Dark Iron dwarves may hide objects of great value... objects that would fit nicely into our family museum.\nMayara says she found something and will need aid in retrieving it, but it is not in Thaurissan. Instead, a foray into Blackrock Spire will be required.\nI do not know the details, but if interested then speak with Mayara in the Burning Steppes.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"You came from Stormwind? Wonderful -- I know of an object of art that Remington would kill to have in his museum, but extracting it won't be easy.\nThat's where you come in.\nStormwind City Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Count Remington Ridgewell","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Mayara Brightwing","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"98286":{"id":98286,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Nasalanna Windsinger","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96046":{"id":96046,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Yarr Hammerstone in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","back":"Yes, I can teach you.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":50,"y":50.4,"n":"Yarr Hammerstone","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96606":{"id":96606,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Lyreena's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94286":{"id":94286,"t":"Craftsmans writ flash bomb","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Flash Bomb\nFlash Bomb","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Flash Bomb, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Flash Bomb Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94286","cats":["crafting"]},"6126":{"id":6126,"t":"Lessons Anew","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"You're now ready to learn about poison and the power we as druids have over it, ‹name›. Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to purge even the most foul of poisons with but a mere incantation. This gift is not to be taken lightly... and to ensure you learn this lesson, you'll work to address the effects of poisonings as a layman would.\nTravel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze; he awaits your arrival to begin your lesson.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Greetings young druid, I'm glad to see you ready and eager to learn about the curing of poisons.\nWhile most druids in the past were put through pre-planned trials, your work will involve no such thing. There has been a rash of animal poisonings at the Crossroads in the Barrens, and they're unable to bring it under control. Someone there has requested Moonglade for aid, so we are sending you there to aid them. This is no exercise - the work you'll do is quite real. Bear this in mind.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22,"n":"Hana Lighthoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.4,"y":27.6,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"926":{"id":926,"t":"Flawed Power Stone","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFlawed Power Stone","done":"These stones are infused with magical energy, but purposefully flawed. They are very unstable and once removed from the table they will consume themselves quickly.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":20,"n":"Flawed Power Stone","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":20,"n":"Flawed Power Stones","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"526":{"id":526,"t":"Lightforge Ingots","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 5 lightforge ingots, then return to Glorin Steelbrow in the Wetlands.\n5 Lightforge Ingot Bluegill Raider 80 %","desc":"You might have found one lightforge ingot in that chest, but that's not enough to craft anything decent!\nYou should go back there and look for more. Maybe the murlocs around that wrecked ship have lightforge ingots on them.","rew":"Experience: 1,750\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you find the lightforge iron you need?","done":"Ah, you found them! Now let's get this lightforge iron hammered into something useful, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1166":{"id":1166,"t":"Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village wants you to retrieve his grog, snuff and strongbox in Dustwallow Swamp.\nMok'Morokk's Snuff Mok'Morokk's Snuff\nMok'Morokk's Grog Mok'Morokk's Grog\nMok'Morokk's Strongbox Mok'Morokk's Strongbox","desc":"Bow before Overlord Mok'Morokk!\nRexxar make me mighty leader of Stonemaul Clan!\nMe good leader. Me keep clan safe.\nBig dragons come and make fire at old home. Me smart ogre. Find new home for clan here.\nLeave old home so fast, me forget stuff. Tiny ‹race›, go get my things. Go south and find my yummy grog, my snuff and my strongbox. Me like you after you do that. You look in Den of Flame and Stonemaul Ruins... they be there, me sure!","rew":"You will receive:\nEnormous Ogre Boots\nExperience: 4,450","back":"Me thirsty for grog. Me miss snuff too. Where is strongbox? You go get for Overlord Mok'Morokk.\nGo find south in old home. Me too busy leading ogres to get.","done":"You good ‹race›. Me miss things very much. Me like you now.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.3,"y":31.4,"n":"Overlord Mok'Morokk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5246":{"id":5246,"t":"Fragments of the Past","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Sacred Highborne Writings in the Temple of Zin-Malor in Azshara, and bring them to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.\nSacred Highborne Writings Sacred Highborne Writings","desc":"I did not realize... Forgive my callous words, ‹class›.\nThe mistakes of my ancestors are not what I wish to dwell on, but if your request is truly genuine, then I will help you.\n<Aurora examines the fragments.>\nI believe this is the Crystal of Zin-Malor, an artifact that can contain and control strong arcane forces. It could have been used for good, but the evil intentions of those that stole it caused it to shatter.\nGo to the Temple of Zin-Malor in Azshara - I can only hope the book is still there.","rew":"Experience: 5,800\n+25 reputation with Alliance","back":"It is only in the pages of the sacred writings that I will be able to discern whether or not I can help you...","done":"The pages have gone untouched for many many years...\nEastern Plaguelands Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":46.5,"y":16,"n":"Aurora Skycaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"46":{"id":46,"t":"Bounty on Murlocs","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Junior's Hunting Bow.","obj":"Bring 8 Torn Murloc Fins to Guard Thomas at the east Elwynn bridge.\n8 Torn Murloc Fin Murloc Lurker 50 % , Murloc Forager 50 %","desc":"The Stormwind Army has placed a bounty on murloc lurkers and foragers in Elwynn. Slaughter them and bring me their torn murloc fins, and the Stormwind Army will reward you well.\nThe murlocs have built a village at Stone Cairn Lake north of here, and another to the south where the stream forks.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLong Bayonet Solid Metal Club Well-used Sword Junior's Hunting Bow\nNew in Forever: Junior's Hunting Bow.\nExperience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"How goes the hunting, ‹name›?","done":"You have the fins? Great! Marshal Dughan is anxious about the Murloc situation in eastern Elwynn, and I'd like to tell him that it's becoming under control.\nYour actions have helped realize that.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3646":{"id":3646,"t":"Membership Card Renewal","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -2g instead of 0.","rew":"You will receive:\nGoblin Engineer Membership Card","back":"In order to renew your membership card, you will need to pay the renewal fee of two gold pieces.","done":"Since you're a practitioner of Goblin engineering and are in good standing, I am able to renew a lapsed membership card for the fee of two gold pieces. Once this fee is paid, you will be reissued a new membership card. This will allow access to Goblin engineering schemata from appropriate trainers.\nThis card will last for two weeks of activity, at the end of which your membership fees will become due again! If you want to access schemata, you'll need to bring your dues out of arrears.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Vazario Linkgrease","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"8446":{"id":8446,"t":"Shrouded in Nightmare","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find someone capable of deciphering the meaning behind the Nightmare Engulfed Object.\nPerhaps a druid of great power could assist you.\nNightmare Engulfed Object Ysondre , Lethon , Emeriss , Taerar\nProvided: Nightmare Engulfed Object","desc":"Corruption seeps from this object.\nThere may be a link between this object and the dragons coming forth from the Dream. You must find someone that can decipher the meaning of this item. Perhaps the druids of the Moonglade or Cenarion Hold could assist you further.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Yes, ‹race›?","done":"I must remove the taint from this object. This may shed some light on my recent failures to delve into the Dream. Give it to me.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1}],"cats":["epic"]},"95646":{"id":95646,"t":"Horrors in the highland","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill a Highland Horror within Excavation Sites and bring its root core to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.\nHorrible Rootcore","desc":"These brackish wetlands hold a greater well of unsalted southern waters. It pains me, yet within my roots I sense a corruption seeping through that mountain gully.\nThe creatures, like those in our lowlands, react more bitterly to the taint. Lacking the sea's hardening salt since life's dawn, they have little strength against such evil.\nGo to those highlands, and bring me the Highland Horror's root core.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIronwood Destroyer Curl of Life Hornbeam Heft\nExperience: 6,150","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.2,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4446":{"id":4446,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":43,"y":47,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5886":{"id":5886,"t":"Salve via Disenchanting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lesser Nether Essence","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.\nI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!","done":"Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, ‹name›. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2766":{"id":2766,"t":"Find OOX-22/FE!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the distress beacon to Oglethorpe's homing robot in a cave near Feral Scar Vale.\nOOX-22/FE Distress Beacon Zapped Cliff Giant 1 % , Zapped Wave Strider 1 % , Zapped Land Walker 1 % , Zapped Shore Strider 1 % and 4 more\nProvided: OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon","desc":"You have uncovered some sort of strange, egg-shaped device made from metal. Fiddling with one of its knobs springs the egg to life, as it opens up into some sort of gnomish robotic contraption! A voice from inside the robotic egg crackles to life.\n\"My name's Oglethorpe Obnoticus, and my homing robot has crashed! I will reward you for its recovery; please take this beacon to the robot!\"\n\"I now have computed the coordinates of the robot for you; it is in a cave near Feral Scar Vale!\"","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken? The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:\n\"Yes, excellent work! This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs. Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover - the beacon will take care of the rest!\"","done":"You place the egg... distress beacon... inside the chicken... homing robot.\nHums and whirs are heard from inside the robot as it struggles to stand up. After the robot comes to life, Oglethorpe's voice is heard once more, but now from inside the robot:\n\"OOX-22/FE is working at least, but it needs major repairs! It is much too heavy for you to carry it... but I think I have an idea. Are you up for watching over it some more?\"","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":53.4,"y":55.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-22/FE","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7726":{"id":7726,"t":"Refuel for the Zapping","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Water Elemental Cores from the Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays along the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, and bring them back to Zorbin Fandazzle who is near the dock there.\n6 Water Elemental Core Sea Elemental 50 % , Sea Spray 50 %","desc":"More work, you say? Did my heroic mission of collecting bits of goo found inside elemental beings not slake your thirst for adventure? Perhaps more of the same will vainly try to fill the bottomless well of questing you possess...\nOK, melodrama aside, I do need more water elemental cores. I'm trying desperately to set up shop here, so the rewards won't be as great... but I promise you I'll tell everyone in earshot how you've helped me. Trust me on this - I know people in the Cartel!","rew":"Money: 21 0 gold, 21 silver, 0 copper Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Have you managed to find the elemental cores I need?","done":"Top notch, ‹name›, top notch! While the coin I give you might not be the most you'll ever receive for such work, rest assured my comrades in the Steamwheedle Cartel will hear about your efforts!\nIf you are looking for anything else to do, then let me know. I can always use more elemental cores and such.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":44.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Zorbin Fandazzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2926":{"id":2926,"t":"Gnogaine","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,950 experience instead of 2,200, 1.8 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Use the Empty Leaden Collection Phial on Irradiated Invaders or Irradiated Pillagers to collect radioactive fallout. Once it is full, take it back to Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.\nFull Leaden Collection Phial\nProvided: Empty Leaden Collection Phial","desc":"Since the accident, all Gnoarn thinks about or talks about is cleansing Gnomeregan of the trogg infestation and finding a cure for the sickness that plagues it, ‹name›.\nLuckily, Razzle and I are close to some kind of cure - either that or the recipe for a really powerful rum. We won't know until we test! Naturally, in order to test our theory, we're going to need a few things; namely, fallout from the irradiated troggs in Gnomeregan. Fill up this phial with the green glow and bring it back!","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,950\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Can't you see we're trying to cure an entire species of gnomes here??! We need more of the green glow!","done":"Excellent work! The time has come to test the new formula. If this works, not only should that captured leper gnome be cured, but I should have a full head of hair! Stand back!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.9,"y":49.4,"n":"Ozzie Togglevolt","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"4606":{"id":4606,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box\nExperience: 2,450","done":"As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt. A simple \"ding\" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward. Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow. The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status. Even if the machine didn't work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.\nWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4606\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"686":{"id":686,"t":"A King's Tribute","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"King Magni Bronzebeard wants you to speak with Grand Mason Marblesten.","desc":"I do not expect good dwarves like Mrs. Balloo to understand why the travesties of war must be endured for the greater good of our people. The loss of her husband, and the loss of every dwarf that fights in the name of the Alliance, weighs heavy on my soul.\nWhile I cannot bring her husband back from the Twisting Nether, I can pay tribute to him.\nI am going to commission a memorial to Sully Balloo to be built by Grand Mason Marblesten.\nSend word to him now, ‹class›. You shall be custodian of my bidding.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"So King Magni Bronzebeard himself sent ye?\nMy, my! This must be important!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.3,"y":35.2,"n":"Grand Mason Marblesten","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"7806":{"id":7806,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Ironforge.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of Ironforge, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":26.2,"n":"Mistina Steelshield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8926":{"id":8926,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Wildheart Belt and a set of Wildheart Gloves Deliana in Ironforge.\nWildheart Belt Scholomance Handler 5.2 % in Scholomance , The Ravenian 4 % in Scholomance , Spectral Teacher 3.8 % in Scholomance , Spectral Researcher 1.5 % in Scholomance and 4 more\nWildheart Gloves Smolderthorn Berserker 4.5 % , Rage Talon Dragonspawn 3.8 % , Firebrand Pyromancer 2.4 % , Scarshield Raider 2.1 % and 4 more","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Belt Feralheart Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9006":{"id":9006,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Helm of Valor and Breastplate of Valor.\nHelm of Valor Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nBreastplate of Valor General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nHelm of Heroism Breastplate of Heroism\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Valor pieces in exchange for your new Helm and Breastplate of Heroism?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8686":{"id":8686,"t":"High Mountain the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.1,"y":57.9,"n":"Elder High Mountain","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"3086":{"id":3086,"t":"Glyphic Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Glyphic Tablet and speak with Mai'ah near the entrance to the Den in the Valley of Trials.\nGlyphic Tablet\nProvided: Glyphic Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ya look to please Mai'ah already, ‹name›. Dat be good. You give Mai'ah respect, and Mai'ah maybe give you respect back. But enough o' dat, you be here to learn 'bout magic, not hear Mai'ah talk.\nThere be only one ting Mai'ah can no teach you 'bout magic, ‹name›, and dat's how to stop da corruptin'.","done":"You be among da most powerful beings on da planet, ‹name›... there no arguin' dat. And everyone know it... know it good, too!\nBut ya must be weary! 'cause it not orc, or elf, or dwarf dat you should be scared of... it be da tings you can'na see. Magic be powerful. Make you do tings you may not want to do. Make ya tink you more powerful then you really be. Be patient. Be smart.\nWhen ya tink you be ready for trainin', come back to Mai'ah. She teach you what you ready to learn, no problem.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.5,"y":69,"n":"Mai'ah","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9326":{"id":9326,"t":"Stealing the Undercity's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much.","obj":"Return the Flame of the Undercity to the Festival Loremaster.\nFlame of the Undercity\nProvided: Flame of the Undercity","desc":"This flame, stolen from the ruins above the Undercity, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Loremaster might know more...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n10 Elderberry Pie 10 Fire-toasted Bun 10 Midsummer Sausage 10 Toasted Smorc\nYou will also receive:\n20 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"Hm... what a strange fire! It is subdued, nearly smoldering, but the heat is intense. And you received this from the Undercity, you say? Fascinating. With the flames of all three cities, who knows what we could accomplish?\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"766":{"id":766,"t":"Mazzranache","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Prairie Wolf Heart, Flatland Cougar Femur, Plainstrider Scale and Swoop Gizzard to Maur Raincaller at Bloodhoof Village.\nPrairie Wolf Heart Prairie Wolf Alpha 10 % , Prairie Stalker 9 % , Prairie Wolf 7 %\nFlatland Cougar Femur Flatland Cougar 7 %\nPlainstrider Scale Ornery Plainstrider 15 % , Fleeting Plainstrider 11 % , Greater Plainstrider 10 % , Mazzranache 9 % and 3 more\nSwoop Gizzard Taloned Swoop 8 % , Swoop 7 % , Wiry Swoop 5 %","desc":"My grandfather told me stories about his battles with a strider named Mazzranache. He told me of its demonic red eyes, razor-sharp talons and venomous bite.\nAs fortune would have it, while traveling across the plains, I encountered it, and it took a nasty bite from my shoulder. He was as terrible as my grandfather described. I will need some hard-to-find animal parts to clean the infection from his bite: a wolf heart, cougar femur, plainstrider scale and swoop gizzard.\nHurry, time is of the essence.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCliff Runner Boots Plains Hunter Wristguards\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"My fever grows worse and I find my mind drifting into delirious nightmares... I should have known that I wouldn't be able to handle a beast my grandfather was unable to defeat...\nDo you have the ingredients for the remedy? I fear if I do not clean the infection soon, it will be the death of me.","done":"Ah, thank you, ‹name›. Using the items you brought me, I will be able to create the remedy I need to stop the spread of the infection and, eventually, cure it completely. I owe you my life in thanks.\nBut I'll never forget that screeching call when Mazzranache came upon me, the blaze of color as its beak descended...\nBe wary on your travels.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":60.8,"n":"Maur Raincaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9086":{"id":9086,"t":"Dreamwalker Tunic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreamwalker Tunic if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Tunic, 25 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 6 Cured Rugged Hides and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Tunic\n25 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n6 Cured Rugged Hide\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Tunic\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Tunic is ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9246":{"id":9246,"t":"Icy Scale Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -300g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 24 Heavy Scorpid Scale, 7 Essence of Water, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.\n8 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n24 Heavy Scorpid Scale\n7 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create an Icy Scale breastplate. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcy Scale Breastplate","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5726":{"id":5726,"t":"Hidden Enemies","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Lieutenant's Insignia to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nLieutenant's Insignia Burning Blade Apprentice 20 % , Burning Blade Fanatic 20 %","desc":"One thing I will not tolerate are traitors in our midst, ‹name›. But I would be a fool to play my hand so early--it would not sufficiently cut the corruption out of our lands and only cause the infection to grow worse.\nBut you, a young adventurer, could go places my agents could not... could learn the truth... could find the true head of the beast.\nIf you are brave enough, then enter Skull Rock to the east of Orgrimmar, find a lieutenant's insignia off one of the Burning Blade there, and return to me.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the insignia yet, ‹name›?\nIt will be a vital tool in you infiltrating what I believe is the greatest threat to the Horde and us finally finding peace in our new home.\nYou will learn how intricate a web men and orcs alike can weave when they are motivated by greed and power. The hidden agendas, the corruption, all of it will become clear. You will find yourself in the midst of a war you never knew existed.","done":"Good, ‹name›! The spirits be praised, perhaps you are the one who will finally put my greatest fears to rest! Who would suspect someone so young and so brave would rise up and champion our cause? You remind me of myself when I was younger. I will ensure that you are justly rewarded for your efforts if we both survive the coming storm.\nBut there is time for more praise later. You've not accomplished anything in comparison to what you will face... but this is a good start.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"97246":{"id":97246,"t":"Meal appeal","lv":15,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Visit Borstan's Firepit and tell him Thatog wants you to deliver Migi's lunch to him personally.","desc":"My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!\nPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.\nDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal.","done":"Of course. Migi's parents and I have an arrangement to give Migi a bagged lunch every day, but I can only ensure the boy gets his food if he actually comes in to pick it up.\nSometimes, he doesn't pick up his meal multiple times a week, and I wonder where he gets the energy to stay out and play.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.6,"y":72,"n":"Thatog","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":57.4,"y":53.4,"n":"Borstan","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"97326":{"id":97326,"t":"Rocks to rests","lv":15,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return 8 Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.\n8 Smooth Boulder","desc":"Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.\nThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.\nYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMogra's Friendship Bracelet Thra's Friendship Bracelet Puk's Friendship Bracelet Brog's Friendship Bracelet Migi's Friendship Bracelet\nExperience: 800\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"It's nice to not have to always sit in the dirt!","done":"How can you even hold all of those boulders!\nThose are great. Most even have a nice flat side, too. Now that you carried them all the way over here we can scoot them around in the dirt, right where we want 'em.\nThanks, Gehrfik!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":36.8,"y":29,"n":"Thra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1646":{"id":1646,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.","desc":"In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.\nAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.\nKnow this well, and never forget it.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Welcome back, ‹name›. You've spent time reading the book, I hope?\nThen you should be prepared to have yourself tested. There are always tasks to be done throughout the city and our lands; acts of compassion and understanding; people who need help; creatures to slay.\nBy proving you have the patience to help others, especially those who are less fortunate, you prove that you are a servant of the Light and of sound mind.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1806":{"id":1806,"t":"The Test of Righteousness","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Jordan Stilwell to finish forging a weapon for you.","desc":"Why don't we go over to the forge and get started on this? I've been preparing for your arrival for some time, so it shouldn't take long at all.\nWhen we're done, you'll be far more prepared to defend the Light than you have been, this much I swear.\nI'll be somewhat honest, ‹name›, seeing the results of your exploits makes me somewhat envious. But knowing that I can contribute to your adventures in my own significant way does bring me some joy.","rew":"You will receive:\nVerigan's Fist\nExperience: 2,200","done":"Here it is, ‹name›. A weapon worthy of a champion of the Light such as yourself. I've named it after a great dwarven paladin who was a friend of mine. His name was Verigan... Bosch Verigan.\nPlease take it on behalf of myself and my wife. We owe you a great debt, and the world will be a safer place with one of your skill traveling the land.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":52.5,"y":36.9,"n":"Jordan Stilwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7646":{"id":7646,"t":"The Divination Scryer","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Azerothian Diamond and a Pristine Black Diamond to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\nAzerothian Diamond Hakkari Thorium Vein 1.2 % , Large Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more\nPristine Black Diamond Veteran Commando 2.3 % , Witherbark Speaker 1 % in Zul'Gurub , Winterax Axe Thrower 1 % , Lady Illucia Barov 1 % in Scholomance and 4 more","desc":"We now must assemble a Divination Scryer - this will begin the trial that will allow you to redeem the fallen charger. Your scryer, actually, is almost done. The exorcism censer used in Terrordale is the catalyst for it, and I will fashion a suitable housing for the device.\nThe last components needed, though, are two diamonds. They must be as juxtaposed in brilliance as they are in purpose - an Azerothian and a Pristine Black. These two will be the beacon by which the scryer will pierce the shadows!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have come so very far, ‹name›. Your final act of worldly-item sacrifice will be the genesis for one of your greatest accomplishments. I can feel it in the very fiber of my being!","done":"These are fine specimens, ‹name› - the final pieces are now in place. At long last, your time has come!\nIn the depths of the Great Ossuary of Scholomance are the skeletal remains of many beings. Amongst them is a once-noble charger. The hollowed soul of this charger now serves as the steed for Death Knight Darkreaver. It is he whom you will face, and it is this steed that you will pass judgment upon. Only you, ‹name›, can redeem its soul and save it from the torment of its servitude.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5646":{"id":5646,"t":"Devouring Plague","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Devouring Plague.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"Aelthalyste show our people great respect by sending them back to me for more training, and now I do the same for her tribe.\nYou return to the Undercity, ‹name›. There, in the War Quarter, she be ready to teach you more 'bout your people and their ways. Go there, and do not wait long.","rew":"You will learn: Devouring Plague\nExperience: 390","done":"Good, you've returned, and not a moment too late. We have great things to discuss, ‹name›. Your abilities are growing stronger, and we must make sure you are ready.\nThunder Bluff Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.6,"y":20.7,"n":"Father Cobb","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"126":{"id":126,"t":"Howling in the Hills","lv":25,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Yowler's Paw to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire.\nYowler's Paw Yowler","desc":"‹name›, the gnolls are still out there. I can hear their baying as they hunt in the hills above Lakeshire. And one cry is louder than the rest - Yowler, their leader.\nKill Yowler and send his pack scattering! Bring me his paw as proof.\nAnd be careful, this gnoll is their leader for a reason. He is no Mongrel...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRing of Iron Will Gold Militia Boots\nExperience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yowler is a dangerous creature, ‹name›. If you're not ready for him, I understand.","done":"Again, thank you for your help. The Stormwind army is so busy dealing with the orcs, they don't have the troops to protect Redridge from local threats like the gnolls.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"2206":{"id":2206,"t":"Snatch and Grab","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Defias Dockmaster and recover the Shipping Schedule for Master Mathias Shaw.\nDefias Shipping Schedule Defias Dockmaster","desc":"Our operatives in the field are reporting heavy Defias activity south of Goldshire. The reports indicate that the Defias have taken over Jerod's Landing and are now using it as a way to smuggle large quantities of contraband from Redridge to Westfall.\nI need you to infiltrate the dock house and get me that shipping schedule, ‹name›. You will probably find it buried deep in the pockets of the Dockmaster.\n...and ‹name›, should you be discovered, SI:7 will disavow all knowledge of your existence.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Cunning\nExperience: 850","back":"Your mortality wanes with every moment you waste loitering in the barracks, ‹class›.","done":"I am astonished... Astonished that Keryn finally found a recruit that could possibly have the makings of a proper ‹class›. Take this blade, ‹name›. A day will come when you will be called upon again to serve the SI:7. Hone your skills, keep your eyes open and that blade sharp.\nYou won't see us coming but you'll feel it when we get there...\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1886":{"id":1886,"t":"The Deathstalkers","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get Astor's Letter of Introduction and return it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter.\nAstor's Letter of Introduction Astor Hadren","desc":"If you wish to join the Deathstalkers, Lord Varimathras' elite guard, you will have to prove your worth.\nI will not lie to you, ‹name›, this task could mean your death.\nI have some things that need attending to. I require the personal effects of Astor Hadren, a messenger who travels between Silverpine and the Undercity. I will leave the method of procurement to your discretion.\nIt will be better for you if you know less of the nature of this business. Succeed and I shall tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 675","back":"Success to report?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. You've passed the first part of this test. Hopefully Andron will not have caught wind of your activities, and we will be able to convince him that you are, in fact, the messenger he is expecting.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3566":{"id":3566,"t":"Rise, Obsidion!","lv":52,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 40 instead of 45. Pays 1g 55s instead of 1g 30s.","obj":"Slay Lathoric the Black and Obsidion, and return to Thorius in Ironforge with the Head of Lathoric the Black and the Heart of Obsidion.\nHead of Lathoric the Black Lathoric the Black\nHeart of Obsidion Obsidion","desc":"It... It... It was all a trap.\nForgive... me.\nKill the bastard... Kill him for us... for Thorius.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCenturion Legplates Lordrec Helmet Ring of Fortitude\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,600\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I don't believe you! Show me proof!","done":"<Thorius' face turns white.>\nThis... this cannot be. My own brother? He set this all up?\n<Thorius' face contorts in anger.>\nHe betrayed me, he betrayed Ironforge! It seems as if the influence of the Old Gods is still strong in these lands. I fear that if my brother - a once noble and honorable man - was so easily turned to the will of Ragnaros, no one is safe.\nSearing Gorge Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Dying Archaeologist","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Curator Thorius","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"92846":{"id":92846,"t":"Outcast necromancers","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay Outcast Necromancers within the Valley of Bones.\nOutcast Necromancer x 6\nMagram Clan Centaur:\nLevel 40 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Quest ID 92846","cats":["shendralas"]},"8286":{"id":8286,"t":"What Tomorrow Brings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Caverns of Time in Tanaris and find Anachronos, Brood of Nozdormu.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"The embrace of death had all but overcome my being when he intervened. He breathed only once upon my maimed body and then waited patiently for the sands of time to cleanse my wounds.\n\"Forever you will remain if you must\", he said, and with those words I was bound as a Watcher.\nLook now to the desert. The second war is upon us. You must seek out the resting place of the Bronze. Venture to the Caverns of Time and see if the master has returned. I must be sure before I am able to proceed.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Has Anachronos returned?","done":"It is as it should be - the great one has risen. My watch comes to an end...\nSilithus Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":36.4,"n":"Baristolth of the Shifting Sands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"446":{"id":446,"t":"Thule Ravenclaw","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Bethor's Scroll to Apothecary Renferrel at the Silverpine Sepulcher.\nBethor's Scroll\nProvided: Bethor's Scroll","desc":"This Ichor was crafted by an old colleague of mine: Thule Ravenclaw. He was a young, promising mage before the great war, but when the Lich King rose to power, he betrayed his brethren and allied with the Scourge.\nI did not realize he still lives, nor that he leads the Rot Hides in their forays against us!\nI know many of his spells, and can help concoct a potion to counter them. Take this scroll back to Apothecary Renferrel. It has the incantations needed for the potion.","rew":"You will receive:\nBethor's Potion\nExperience: 290\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. What did Bethor have to say?","done":"This scroll is laced with powerful magic. I've never used such forces in a potion ... it will be a powerful mixture, and should serve you well should you attack Thule in his stronghold on Fenris Isle.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1006":{"id":1006,"t":"What lies beyond","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 18 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 14 16 21 25 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 1006","cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1246":{"id":1246,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Dashel Stonefist in Stormwind.","desc":"Yeah, now that I think about it... Dashel... Dashel something... What was his name? FIST! Dashel Stonefist. They call him Fist in some circles--probably on account that he likes to get in brawls.\nYou can find him in Old Town usually--right smack dab in the center of it. Go talk to him. If you have to, use a sword or something heavy and blunt to persuade him to open up some. And don't hesitate. If he's in this as deep as these papers suggest, then he's not going to give you any information willingly.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"What?!\nYou come into me alley and ask questions about me personal business? Business which you obviously have nothing to do with.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":74.3,"y":59.2,"n":"Dashel Stonefist","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"606":{"id":606,"t":"Scaring Shaky","lv":41,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,300 experience instead of 825, 4 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring 5 Mistvale Giblets to \"Shaky\" Phillipe in Booty Bay.\n5 Mistvale Giblets Elder Mistvale Gorilla 30 %","desc":"If there's one thing I can't stand, it's people who don't pay their gambling debts! And there are a lot of people who owe me. Think you can help me collect?\nFirst, there's \"Shaky\" Phillipe down by the docks. He owes me plenty after last week's game and I want my due! But to get it, we'll have to scare him.\nGo out of town and hunt Elder Mistvale Gorillas. Find a nice selection of giblets, then take them to Shaky. Don't let on that they're from an animal; let him think the worst.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+25 reputation with Booty Bay\n-125 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Hey! I don't like the look you're giving me, mister.","done":"Ack! Where'd you get these? No, don't tell me. I don't want to know!\nWho sent you? Sea Wolf?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":73.6,"n":"\"Shaky\" Phillipe","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"206":{"id":206,"t":"Mai'Zoth","lv":46,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Mind's Eye to Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp.\nMind's Eye Mai'Zoth","desc":"Kurzen may be dead, but...that which drove him to evil still lives! Through my studies I have discovered this: An Ogre Mage - Mai'Zoth - dwells in an Ogre Mound within the eastern mountains of Stranglethorn. He is rumored to employ mind-controlling magic, and I am positive that he corrupted Kurzen.\nIf Mai'Zoth is allowed to live, then his evil may influence others, and may even cause another Kurzen to surface.\nKill him, and bring me his Mind's Eye, the artifact he uses to corrupt others.","rew":"You will receive:\nTranquil Orb\nExperience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I give you my blessing. Mai'Zoth's strength is matched only by his evil.","done":"Aha! You've done it! You are a great force for good, ‹name›, and may your strength never fade!\nI will study this Mind's Eye and determine if it may be used for good. If not... then it must be destroyed.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.8,"y":3.6,"n":"Brother Nimetz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8366":{"id":8366,"t":"Southsea Shakedown","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Security Chief Bilgewhizzle of Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris wants you to kill 10 Southsea Pirates, 10 Southsea Freebooters, 10 Southsea Dock Workers and 10 Southsea Swashbucklers.\nSouthsea Pirate slain : 0/ 10\nSouthsea Freebooter slain : 0/ 10\nSouthsea Dock Worker slain : 0/ 10\nSouthsea Swashbuckler slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Argh! They want the impossible from me!\nThe Steamwheedle Cartel wants me to teach the Southsea pirates a lesson. The problem is that I can't be in two places at once; I need to stay here to keep the peace.\nOf late, the pirates have been disregarding the protection money that the cartel regularly forks over. So I'd like to temporarily deputize you to go down there and show them what for.\nYou'll find them at Lost Rigger Cove, which is not too far to the south. Thanks ‹name›, I'll owe you one!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSouthsea Head Bucket Southsea Mojo Boots\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Back so soon? I hope you taught those Southsea hoodlums a lesson they won't soon forget.","done":"‹name›! You are the man!!!\nI'm sure that the Cartel will ease up on me now that you've dealt with those Southsea scum. Let's see, what can I give you as a reward? How about a little coin and you choose from one of these for your trouble?","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":23.9,"n":"Security Chief Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2606":{"id":2606,"t":"In Good Taste","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Marin Noggenfogger wants you to speak with Sprinkle in Gadgetzan.\nThistleshrub Dew\nProvided: Thistleshrub Dew","desc":"Blech! This stuff tastes terrible! So much for that idea...\nWait, what's that? Oh, I know, I know, you think I shouldn't give up on this stuff. Well, okay then.\nUhhhh, I have an idea! Brilliant! Take this dew to my friend Sprinkle -- she's an excellent chef. Tell her what we're up to here and that we want to make it go down a little easier.\nI mean, if it's going to taste that bad, it at least should have some kick to it... And I'm just not feeling it...","rew":"Experience: 460","back":"So old Marin's up to it again, eh? What's this concoction made from?","done":"Marin's a good guy, don't get me wrong -- just a little... eccentric, I'd say.\nAnd of course he needs my help, yet again.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":28.7,"n":"Marin Noggenfogger","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.1,"y":26.9,"n":"Sprinkle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8606":{"id":8606,"t":"Decoy!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris wants you to travel to Winterspring and place the Bag of Gold at the drop off point documented by the booknappers.\nWho Does Number Two Work For?\nProvided: Narain's Special Kit","desc":"I've got it! Here's what we're going to do. I'm going to fill a sack up with rocks and you're going to make the drop. I know it said that I should make the delivery and I'm going to - sort of.\n<Narain looks you up and down.>\nYes, you will do just fine. Take this turban, robe, and sack of rocks and head to the drop off point in Winterspring.\nI've included everything you need in this special kit. When they show up to pick up the goods, snuff them out! That will teach them to mess with Narain!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+25 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"I think we may have underestimated these booknappers.\nTanaris Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8766":{"id":8766,"t":"The Changing of Paths - Conqueror No More","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\n15 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","back":"Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.","done":"Be well, ‹name›. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"98046":{"id":98046,"t":"Crown of the earth","lv":11,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Drained Vessel to Lariia in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.\nProvided: Drained Vessel","desc":"<Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm's gaze narrows.>\nYou're still here?\nTake the phial and get out of my sight, ‹class›. It is clear my answers do not lie in the waters, just as they did not before.\nPerhaps one of the priestesses in the Temple of the Moon to the south will dispose of it.\n<Fandral looks away, no longer speaking to you.>\nI must look elsewhere if this is to work...","back":"How may I aid you?","done":"Do not mind the Arch Druid, Sneaky. He bears the weight of much in Malfurion's absence.\nWait! Some drops yet remain in the phial! Perhaps that is why his incantation failed?","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":8.8,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.2,"y":88.4,"n":"Lariia","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"846":{"id":846,"t":"Revenge of Gann","lv":26,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gann Stonespire wants you to bring him 6 vials of Nitroglycerin, 6 bundles of Wood Pulp, and 6 samples of Sodium Nitrate.\n6 Nitroglycerin Lord Cyrik Blackforge 40 % , Bael'dun Officer 40 % , Bael'dun Rifleman 40 % , Bael'dun Soldier 40 %\n6 Wood Pulp Lord Cyrik Blackforge 40 % , Bael'dun Officer 40 % , Bael'dun Rifleman 40 % , Bael'dun Soldier 40 %\n6 Sodium Nitrate Lord Cyrik Blackforge 40 % , Bael'dun Officer 40 % , Bael'dun Rifleman 40 % , Bael'dun Soldier 40 %","desc":"It is clear the prospector depended on explosives and those noisy vehicles to rip the ground apart. We can expect a new foreman to take over soon.\nI want to give the dwarves a taste of their own medicine. According to these plans if we combine nitroglycerin with wood pulp and sodium nitrate we can create an explosive charge. The rifleman, soldiers and officers in the Keep are known to have the supplies.\nCollect these items and bring them to me. I will fashion a charge that the dwarves won't forget!","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I see you are back, ‹name›.\nWhile Khazgorm's death might delay the digging in my ancestral lands some, it will by no means bring a total end to the destruction.\nThe Keep at Bael Modan is an increasing military threat. Built to defend the dig site, it is now poised for offensive force as well.\nIf you have the ingredients I requested, I can fashion a charge that will make the hasty dwarves reconsider their actions here in the Barrens.","done":"I see you are quite industrious, ‹class›.\nNo doubt we shall soon have a fitting surprise for those dwarves.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.9,"y":77,"n":"Gann Stonespire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1086":{"id":1086,"t":"The Flying Machine Airport","lv":23,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Toxic Fogger to the Venture Co. sky port, then return to Apothecary Zamah.\nProvided: Toxic Fogger","desc":"The toxin is ready. All that remains is its delivery. You, ‹name›, must make that delivery.\nThe Venture Company must have a means of sending messages and light cargo between its headquarters and its operations in Stonetalon. It is likely a small sky port -- not big enough for a zeppelin, but perhaps for a flying machine. You must search the areas in Stonetalon under control of the Venture Company and find this sky port, if it exists. If you find it, then place the toxin there.\nPlace it, and run.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"You must find the Venture Company airport if it exists, ‹name›.","done":"You found the port? Well done, ‹name›! I am sure the goblins were quite surprised from your delivery! Let us hope that toxin finds its way to their headquarters.\nYou have served your people well, and I advise you to ignore any guilt you might harbor for poisoning the Venture Company. They are deserving of far worse.\nAnd if there is one mote of wisdom the Forsaken might teach its allies, it is this:\nDo not shy from dark paths... if those paths lead to victory.\nThunder Bluff Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"366":{"id":366,"t":"Return the Book","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Gunther's Spellbook to him, on the island of Gunther's Retreat.\nGunther's Spellbook\nProvided: Gunther's Spellbook","desc":"Long ago Gunther and I, along with the now Scourge Necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, were friends and students within the Kirin Tor - a society of mages in Dalaran.\nGunther and I both fell to the Plague, but I thought he either remained dead, or was raised into the ranks of the Lich King. It is good to know he is free.\nWe must have him. I have placed a spell on his book that, when he sees it, will show him that I too am free of the Lich King. After knowing this, it is my hope that he will join us.","rew":"Experience: 350\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Your masters are fools to send you here, for I will never again be a Scourge slave!","done":"My book?!? So you were the thief who stole it!\nBut...what is this new enchantment upon it...Bethor? He is in Lordaeron?\nIf he still exists, then perhaps he too escaped from the Lich King's grasp...\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":68.2,"y":41.9,"n":"Gunther Arcanus","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1486":{"id":1486,"t":"Deviate Hides","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,100 experience instead of 1,600, 1.94 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Nalpak in the Wailing Caverns wants 20 Deviate Hides.\n20 Deviate Hide Deviate Coiler 80 % , Deviate Stinglash 80 % , Deviate Creeper 80 % , Deviate Slayer 80 % and 4 more","desc":"As Naralex descended deeper into his nightmare, a strange breed of beasts arose from beneath the Barrens into the Wailing Caverns.\nThese deviate creatures have strange, otherworldly properties. While evil in nature, it is my opinion that some good can come from their existence here in Kalimdor. I believe their hides will be of particular use in the ways of leatherworking.\nIf you feel up to the task, venture into the caves below and retrieve some deviate hides.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeviate Hide Pack Slick Deviate Leggings\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,100","back":"I am very interested in examining the hides from the deviate creatures who have infested these caves. Have you had any luck in collecting some, ‹class›?","done":"Your efforts shall not go unnoticed in gathering these hides, ‹name›.\nThank you for your dedication.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46,"y":35.7,"n":"Nalpak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"5406":{"id":5406,"t":"Corruptor's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Corruptor's Scourgestone Darkmaster Gandling , Marduk Blackpool in Scholomance , Hed'mush the Rotting , Lord Darkscythe and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes!\nOn behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia. Use caution in acquiring one, ‹name› - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nTo acquire a valor token in such a manner indicates that you are a true hero in the cause of good. We value all effort brought to bear against the Scourge, but to take down one of their leaders is to truly deliver onto them a crushing defeat!\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Argent Officer Garush","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5166":{"id":5166,"t":"Breastplate of the Chromatic Flight","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To forge the Breastplate of the Chromatic Flight, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor':\n1 Chromatic Carapace.\n10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales.\n10 Blood of Heroes.\n10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings.\nItem #12871\n10 Brilliant Chromatic Scale\n10 Blood of Heroes\n10 Frayed Abomination Stitching","desc":"The forging of a powerful breastplate to protect against the unrelenting attacks of the chromatic flight is one built upon irony.\nThe scales of the very beasts we battle must be sewn to the pristine carapace of an elder chromatic drake or dragon. None are known to exist at this time and we should hope that none will ever exist.\nLastly, perhaps the most difficult of all components: the blood of heroes.\nThe Sculptor must ultimately forge this creation.","rew":"You will receive:\nBreastplate of the Chromatic Flight\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You have chosen wisely, ‹race›.","done":"Do you not yet understand? The journey was the destination. Can you not feel the battle scars? The pain you underwent?\nHaving survived the ordeal, you are a more powerful being. Much more powerful. This breastplate is merely a reflection of your own innate abilities.\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.3,"y":66.6,"n":"Catalogue of the Wayward","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Jeziba","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"286":{"id":286,"t":"Return the Statuette","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Karl Boran the Menethil Statuette.\nMenethil Statuette\nProvided: Menethil Statuette","desc":"After pulling the barrel free from the muck and opening it, a silvery figurine is found packed in fine straw. It depicts a young, long-haired Paladin with hammer upraised.\nThis must be the Menethil Statuette! You must now return it to Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIcicle Rod Mariner Boots\nExperience: 1,500\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have the statuette?","done":"The captain of the Blind Princess will be relieved to hear this precious cargo has been recovered. You have well earned this payment for services rendered.\nIt is good to see dependable folk like you, especially in trying times such as these.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.9,"y":34.8,"n":"Half-buried Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.3,"y":58.6,"n":"Karl Boran","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"5086":{"id":5086,"t":"Toxic Horrors","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,800 experience instead of 4,134, 1.4 times as much.","obj":"Collect 3 Toxic Horror Droplets for Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\n3 Toxic Horror Droplet Toxic Horror 80 %","desc":"I've studied the sample you returned with, and while I can't say for sure, I believe it contains traces of toxic elements. However, the only way to know for sure is to gather some as a comparison.\nI believe that the Deadwood furbolg may be gathering these elements from other corrupted creatures in Felwood; in particular, the elementals living in the Irontree Woods, called toxic horrors.\nCollect a few samples for me to compare, but be careful -- it's very dangerous there!","rew":"Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"I think we are beginning to uncover what is happening here, ‹name›.","done":"I have to compare this to the substance you found in the cauldron, and then I'm sure we'll know more.\nWinterspring Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"6606":{"id":6606,"t":"A Little Luck","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Now for the Horde only.","obj":"Speak with Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook.","desc":"We can always use a little luck, eh? A small advantage is all it takes to turn things in your favor...\nI happened to make the acquaintance of a rather eccentric witch doctor some time back. She made me a lucky charm... for a price. Believe me, though, it was well worth it!\nMaybe you'd be interested in one of your own? Find Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook. I'm not giving mine up!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ah, so Harlo be sendin' you? Well, den, who might you be? I s'pose you be wantin' my help?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.1,"y":38.4,"n":"Harlo Wigglesworth","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"2846":{"id":2846,"t":"Tiara of the Deep","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tiara of the Deep to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nTiara of the Deep Hydromancer Velratha in Zul'Farrak","desc":"Long ago I possessed a beautiful piece of jewelry, the Tiara of the Deep. And not only was it pretty--it held great power for those with the knowledge to use it.\nSo when word of the tiara reached the Hydromancer Velratha, she had to have it. She sent agents to my home and they stole it while I was away. The thieves!\nI want my tiara back! Go to Zul'Farrak, the troll city in Tanaris, find Velratha and wrench the tiara from her. Return it to me and you'll earn my favor.","rew":"You will receive:\nSpellshifter Rod Gemshale Pauldrons\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,050","back":"Do you have the tiara, ‹name›? Has Velratha learned the price of crossing me?","done":"Wonderful! You found it! And what's just as important--Velratha no longer has it! Thank you, ‹name›. I am forever in your debt!\nAnd if I sounded a little... mean before, pay it no mind. You'll find me a much nicer person to those who haven't stolen from me.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8046":{"id":8046,"t":"The Heathen's Brand","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Heathen's Brand","rew":"You will receive:\nHeathen's Brand\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I may have been too hasty in my judgement, ‹class›. It seems as if your blind faith in this Light has some value after all.\nGive me your brand and I shall amplify its power.","done":"Do what you must to defeat our enemies, ‹class›. Even if it means channeling the Light.\n<Jin'rokh shudders.>","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});